\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

We introduced Causal Style Decomposition (CSD), a black-box framework for detecting per-axis style bias in LLM judges.
Across two judges and two primary style axes, with exploratory evidence on a third, CSD reveals the Likert Blindspot---a two-layer measurement limitation confirmed by seven statistical methods as inherent to Likert scoring, not an artifact of any particular test.
Style bias audits should adopt pairwise comparison as the default protocol; existing Likert-based null findings may reflect measurement insensitivity rather than genuine absence of bias.
Future work should extend CSD to additional judges, axes, and benchmarks.

